---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.ts';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Percentage Calculator handles your data: calculations stay in your browser, no accounts, and no analytics or advertising cookies at present."
  path="/privacy-policy"
  h1="Privacy policy"
  crumbLabel="Privacy policy"
  updated="13 September 2026"
  intro="The short version: your calculations never leave your browser, and this site does not currently set cookies or run analytics."
>
  <div class="prose-site">
    <h2>Your calculations</h2>
    <p>
      Every calculator on this site runs entirely in your browser. The numbers you type are processed
      on your own device by JavaScript that was downloaded with the page. They are not transmitted to
      this site or to any third party, and there is no server-side component that could receive them.
    </p>

    <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Two things may be saved in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>, which is storage local to
      your device that this site can read back on your next visit:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Recent calculations</strong> — up to twelve, so they are still there if you return.
        The “Clear” button next to the list removes them immediately.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your currency symbol preference</strong> on the discount calculator.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This data stays on your device. It is never uploaded, and clearing your browser's site data
      removes it. If storage is unavailable — in a private window, for example — the calculators work
      exactly as normal without it.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not set cookies. There are no advertising cookies, no tracking pixels and no
      third-party embeds.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      No analytics service is running on this site at present, and no analytics scripts are loaded. If
      privacy-respecting analytics are added in future, this page will be updated before they go live
      to say what is collected. Any such measurement would record page visits and which calculators
      are used — never the numbers you enter.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      Like virtually all websites, the hosting provider that serves these pages keeps standard access
      logs, which typically include IP addresses, timestamps, requested URLs and browser user-agent
      strings. These are generated by the hosting infrastructure for security and reliability
      purposes, and are not used to build any profile of you.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Fonts are self-hosted and served from this domain, so loading a page does not make requests to
      Google Fonts or any other external service. The site loads no third-party scripts.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a general-purpose calculator and does not knowingly collect personal information
      from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Because no personal data is collected through this site, there is no account to access, no
      profile to correct and no record to delete. Data stored locally in your browser is under your
      control and can be cleared at any time through the “Clear” button or your browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the “last updated” date above will change with it. Material changes —
      such as introducing analytics or advertising — will be described here before they take effect.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</ContentLayout>
